      <div type="clause" n="15.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 15.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="318" ed="#liebermann"/>And se ðe unlage rære<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.12"/> oððe undom<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.13-2"/> gedeme heonon forð, for læððe oððe for<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.14-2"/> feohfange, beo se wið þone<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.15-2"/> cingc CXX scyll' scyldig on Engla lage<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.16-2"/>, butan he mid aðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.17-2"/> cyðan durre, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hit na<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.18-2"/> rihtor ne cuþe, ⁊ þolige aa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.19-2"/> his þegnscipes, butan he hine æt þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> cingce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.20-2"/> eft<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.dagger"/> gebicge, swa he hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> geþafian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="§" target="#missing"/><pb n="318" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se ðe unlage rǽre oððe undóm gedeme heónan forð, for læððe oððe for feohfange, beo se wið ðone cyng hundtwelftig scill' scyldig on Engla láge, buton he míd aðe cyðan durre, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hít na rihtor ne cuðe, ⁊ ðolie áá his þegenscipes, butan he híne æt ðam cýng<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.3-2"/> gebycge, swa hé him geðafian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="318" ed="#liebermann"/>And se ðe unlage rære oððe undom gedeme heonon forð, for læððe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.2-2"/> oððe feohfangce, beo se wið þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.1-2"/> cyningc his weores<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.3-3"/> scyldig on Engla lage, buton he mid aðe cyðan durre, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hit nan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.3-3"/> rihtor ne cuðe, ⁊ þolige á his ðegenscypes, buton he hine æt þam cyninge gebicge, swa he hym þafian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-d-frags"><pb n="318" ed="#liebermann"/>And se ðe unlaga arære óððe undo<hi rend="italic">m</hi> deme heonan forð, for læððe oððe feohfange, beo se wið þone cyngc CXX scill' scildig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.1"/>,</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="319" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis ammodo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.13"/> (deinceps) únlagam (id est non<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.14"/> legem) erigat uel iniustum iudicium iudicet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.15"/>, pro lesione uel aliqua pecunię<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.16"/> susceptione, sit erga regem CXX solid. reus in Anglorum laga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.17"/> (lege), nisi cum iuramento audeat inueritare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.18"/>, quod hoc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.19"/> rectius nesciuit, et dignitatem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.20"/> suam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.21"/> legalitatis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.star"/> semper<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.22"/> amiserit, nisi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.23"/> (si non) eam redimat erga regem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.24"/>, sicut ei permittet.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="319" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis iniustas leges adinuerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.18-3"/> et iudicauerit, aut causa odii aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.19-3"/> adquisitionis pecunię, sit reus regi XL<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.20-3"/> sol. in lege Anglorum, nisi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.21-2"/> iuramento affirmauerit, se rectius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.22-2"/> iudicare nescisse, et postea careat liberalitate<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.23-2"/> sua, nisi eam á rege<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.oe.24-2"/> redimat ad uelle regis.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="319" ed="#liebermann"/>Quicunque aut iniusticiam statuerit aut iniustum iudicium amodo iudicauerit siue propter odium siue propter munus, sit reus aduersus regem CXX solid. secundum legem Anglorum, nisi iuramento asserere audeat, se rectius discernere nescisse; dignitate sua tamen omni tempore careat, nisi illam a rege iuxta eius libitum redimere ualuerit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="15a.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="180" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ se ðe unlage rǽre oððe undóm gedeme héonan forð, for læððe oððe for feohfange, beo se wið ðone cyng hundtwelftig scill'<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#IICn_15-1.robnote.fn.11"/> scyldig on Engla láge, buton he míd aðe cyðan durre, þæt he hít na rihtor ne cuðe, ⁊ ðolie áá his þegenscipes, butan he híne æt ðam cýng gebycge<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#IICn_15-1.robnote.fn.12"/>, swa he him geðafian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="260" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And se ðe unlage rære oððe undom gedeme heonon forð, for læððe oððe for feohfange, beo se wið þone cingc CXX scyllinga scyldig on Engla lage—butan he mid aðe cyðan durre, þæt he hit na rihtor ne cuþe—and þolige aa his þegnscipes, butan he hine æt þam cingce eft gebicge, swa he him geþafian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="319" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.de.1"/> wer hinfort falsche Satzung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.de.2"/>(-gen <hi rend="italic">D</hi>?) aufstellt oder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.de.3"/> falsch Urtheil ertheilt aus Hass<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.de.4"/> oder für (<hi rend="italic">fehlt A D</hi>) Geldempfang<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.de.5"/>, der sei nach Engländer-Recht gegenüber dem König 120 Schill. (sein Wergeld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_15-1.lnote.de.6"/> <hi rend="italic">A</hi>) schuldig — ausser wenn er durch Eid zu erweisen wagt, dass er es nicht richtiger wusste — und verliere immer seine Thegnwürde [sammt Gerichtshoheit], ausser wenn er sie (wieder <hi rend="italic">G</hi>) vom König auslöst, so wie dieser ihm zu gestatten geruht.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And whoever henceforth sets up an unjust law (laws, D?) or gives a false judgment out of hatred or for (lacking in A D) a bribe, let him be liable to the king for 120 shillings (his wergild, A) under English law — unless he dares to declare on oath that he did not know how to do it more justly — and lose his thegnly rank [with his jurisdiction] for ever, unless he buys it back (again, G) from the king, as the king is willing to permit him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="181" ed="#robertson"/>And he who henceforth promotes injustice or pronounces unjust judgments<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15-1.robnote.n.2"/>, as the result of malice or bribery, shall forfeit 120 shillings<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15-1.robnote.n.3"/> to the king, in districts under English law, unless he is prepared to declare on oath that he did not know how to give a more just verdict<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_15-1.robnote.n.4"/>, and he shall lose for ever his rank as a thegn, unless he redeem it from the king, provided the latter is willing to allow him to do so.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#IICn_15-1.whinote.n.9"/><pb n="464" ed="#whitelock"/>And he who promotes an abuse or gives a wrong judgment henceforth, owing to hatred or bribery, is then to forfeit 120 shillings to the king in the area under English law, unless he dare declare on oath that he knew not how to do it more justly; and he is always to forfeit his thegnly status,<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#IICn_15-1.whinote.n.10"/> unless he may redeem it from the king, according as he will allow him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="261" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And anyone henceforth who promotes injustice or hands down unjust judgments, either because of bias or bribery, shall be liable to the king for one hundred twenty shillings in areas under English law—unless he can declare under oath that he did not know how to deliver a more just sentence—and he shall forfeit forever his rights as a thane, unless he redeems it from the king if he is willing to permit it.</ab>
